4. Removed the translation dependencies and mocking
5. Kept the error boundary and suspense for safety
6. Simplified the component structure while maintaining the core functionality

This approach should resolve the dynamic import error by:
1. Avoiding the async page component entirely
2. Using direct imports instead of dynamic ones
3. Maintaining the core functionality of displaying icons
4. Removing dependencies on Next.js specific features

The component should now render properly without the dynamic import issues. Let me know if you encounter any other errors.

